# Copy to scripts/scan-secrets.local.sh (that path is gitignored) and fill in the
# patterns that identify YOUR deployment: a private address prefix you would not want
# named in a public repo, an internal port, an internal binary or service name.
# scan-secrets.sh reads the single assignment below as data -- it never sources or
# executes this file (that is deliberate: see scripts/lib-env.sh for the reason).
#
# The gate exits 2 with "INCOMPLETE" when no site rules file is present, so a missing
# file cannot be mistaken for a clean scan.
#
# Replace the placeholders below with patterns for YOUR deployment. Keep them escaped
# for `grep -E` (e.g. a private prefix such as 192\.168\. or an internal port). The
# scanner skips this file (and scripts/scan-secrets.local.sh) so a rules file does not
# report itself; do not rely on that to hide a real address in ordinary source.
SITE_ENDPOINT_RULE=YOUR_PRIVATE_PREFIX|YOUR_INTERNAL_PORT|YOUR_SERVICE_NAME
